<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <actionCalls>
        <description>The single entry point for an activated order. submitOrder generates the billing schedules and triggers assetization, and it decomposes the order first when a ProductFulfillmentDecompRule applies. Do not chain createOrUpdateAssetFromOrder after it: that assetizes a second time.</description>
        <name>Submit_Order</name>
        <label>Submit Order</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <actionName>submitOrder</actionName>
        <actionType>submitOrder</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>orderId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>submitOrder</nameSegment>
        <offset>0</offset>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <description>Overrides the standard Order-to-Asset flow, which called submitOrder and then createOrUpdateAssetFromOrder in sequence. Both trigger assetization, so an activation could raise two runs and apply an amendment's quantity delta twice. Dropping submitOrder instead was worse: it is also what generates and maintains the billing schedules, so billing went silent while assets looked correct. Only submitOrder remains. It covers every case — decomposition when a ProductFulfillmentDecompRule matches an order product or its classification, billing schedule generation, and assetization — which is why chaining a second assetizing action was the defect all along.</description>
    <decisions>
        <description>Check if the order has an AppUsageType of RevenueLifecycleManagement before submitting it. Otherwise do nothing.</description>
        <name>IsRevenueLifecycleManagement</name>
        <label>Is RevenueLifecycleManagement</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Record is not RevenueLifecycleManagement</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>RecordIsRevenueLifecycleManagement</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_ApplicationUsageAssignment.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Submit_Order</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Record is RevenueLifecycleManagement</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>RLM Submit Order on Activation {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>RLM Submit Order on Activation</label>
    <overriddenFlow>revenue_o2aflows__o2aFlow</overriddenFlow>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordLookups>
        <description>Get ApplicationUsageAssignment from the updated order.</description>
        <name>Get_ApplicationUsageAssignment</name>
        <label>Get ApplicationUsageAssignment</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>IsRevenueLifecycleManagement</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>RecordId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>AppUsageType</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>RevenueLifecycleManagement</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>AppUsageAssignment</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <start>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Status</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Activated</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Order</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Update</recordTriggerType>
        <scheduledPaths>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_ApplicationUsageAssignment</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <pathType>AsyncAfterCommit</pathType>
        </scheduledPaths>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
